    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_otl_121'), 'On the submit path of the API, which runs with LOG_LEVEL=info in production:

this.logger.debug(
  { tests: summarizeResults(result.tests), code: submission.code },
  "grading payload",
);

A CPU profile of POST /submissions in production shows summarizeResults at 6% of the handler''s time.

Statement: "This line writes nothing in production, yet summarizeResults still runs on every request."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. JavaScript evaluates the arguments before it calls logger.debug, so the object literal is built and summarizeResults runs on every request; only then does the disabled debug method return without serializing or writing anything. The profile confirms it. Guard expensive arguments with a level check (if (this.logger.isLevelEnabled("debug")) { ... } in pino) or remove the line. The misconception is that a filtered level is free: filtering saves the serialization and the bytes, not the work you put into the arguments.', 2, 5
