Fix deployed: the callback passed to this.plagiarism.check is wrapped with context.bind(context.active(), ...).

Statement: "To verify it, check a new trace of POST /submissions: plagiarism.check should be a child from about 66 ms to 866 ms, the root''s self time should drop from about 800 ms to a few milliseconds, new root spans named plagiarism.check should stop appearing, and the plagiarism verdict log line should carry the request''s trace_id."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Each check matches one symptom in the evidence: the child closes the hole in A, the self time measures that nothing else is missing, the orphan count from B should drop to zero for requests served by the new version, and the log line from C proves the callback now runs in the request''s context. Add a regression test with an in-memory exporter (two concurrent submissions, each check under its own request) so the next refactor of the client cannot bring the hole back. The misconception is to verify by eye on a single trace and stop there.', 6, 5
