-- challenge chal_coding_otl_222 (fix_bug)
INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_otl_222', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'observability-opentelemetry'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'observability-opentelemetry') AND order_index = 2 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-otl-2-2' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'find-the-missing-800ms', 'Find the Missing 800 ms', 'Since the plagiarism check was added, traces of POST /submissions on CodeDev have a hole: the root span is 1,240 ms long but its children cover about 440 ms, and every request also creates a separate trace whose root is "plagiarism.check", with the same submission id and the same timing. The trace report has a second problem: its self time column shows negative or too small values for spans whose children run in parallel or keep running after the span ends.

The file contains a context API on top of AsyncLocalStorage (context.active(), context.with(), context.bind(); await and promises carry the context by themselves), a tiny tracer, a fake clock and the plagiarism client, which keeps one connection and calls your callback from code that runs outside any request. Fix the app code so that:
- every plagiarism.check span is a child of the POST /submissions span of the request that made the call, also when several requests are in flight;
- selfTime returns the part of the span''s own [start..end] that none of its children covers: overlapping children count once, and the part of a child outside its parent does not count.

Input (stdin): { "submissions": [{ "id", "startAt", "plagiarismMs", "steps" }] }. A step is "name:ms" (a span with ms of fake I/O), "plagiarism" (the plagiarism check, at most one per submission), "&<step>" (started but not awaited) or an array of steps run with Promise.all.
Output: every trace as a tree, one span per line: name, the submission id when the span has one, [start..end] in fake ms and self=<self time>; children sorted by start, then end, then name. Do not change the context, the tracer, the clock, the plagiarism client or the test runner.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'fix_bug', 30, true, false)
