count(codedev_submissions_total) => 87,400

The team dashboard only shows totals and uses:
sum without (user_id, url) (rate(codedev_submissions_total[5m]))

Statement: "Because the dashboard query removes user_id and url with sum without (...), those series are not stored, so the bill will drop back once this panel is saved."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Labels are attached when the counter is recorded, in the API process: every combination of user_id, url, method and status is exported, scraped, indexed and stored as its own series before any query runs. sum without (...) aggregates at query time; it changes what the panel shows, not what the backend keeps, and it even makes every refresh of the panel read the 87,400 series. To stop paying for them you have to stop recording the labels (or drop them in the SDK with a View, or in the collector, before export). The misconception is that a query decides what is stored.', 1, 5
