if (req.userId) {
  analytics.track({ name: "submission_created", userId: req.userId, properties: { challengeId: req.challengeId, status } });
}

The admin page "Top submitters this week" now reads the submission_created events from the analytics warehouse.

Statement: "After this change codedev_submissions_total stays at a handful of series however many learners submit, and the per-learner question is answered from the events, which are built to hold one row per submission."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Each label now has a small, fixed set of values: one route template for this handler, one method and at most five status classes, so the counter has at most about five series whether CodeDev has a thousand learners or a million. The learner id has not disappeared: it moved to an event, where one row per submission is the normal shape and where a query like "top 10 learners this week" is cheap. The misconception is that dropping user_id from the metric means losing the per-learner answer; it means asking the store that is designed for it.', 2, 5
