-- challenge chal_coding_otl_332 (fix_bug)
INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_otl_332', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'observability-opentelemetry'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'observability-opentelemetry') AND order_index = 3 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-otl-3-3' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'spot-the-ai-mistake-user-id-label', 'Spot the AI Mistake: user_id as a metric label', 'The request sent to an AI coding assistant was: "Add a metric so we can see which learners submit the most." The assistant added a counter, codedev_submissions_total, to the submit handler (POST /submissions) with the labels user_id, url (the raw URL with its query string), method and status (the exact code), and a topLearners(n) for the admin dashboard that sums the counter by user_id. The totals were right, the tests passed and the pull request was merged. Three weeks later the metrics bill had tripled: the counter had one series per learner, per challenge, per query string and per status code, and it grew with every new learner.

Fix SubmissionMetrics:
- the counter keeps only bounded labels: route (the route template matched by the router, req.route), method, and status_class (the first digit of the response status + "xx", for example "4xx");
- per-learner counts go to the analytics sink provided in the file: for each submission by a signed-in learner, call analytics.track({ name: "submission_created", userId, properties: { challengeId, status } }); a request without a userId (an expired session answered with 401) is counted in the metric but not sent to analytics;
- topLearners(n) answers from the sink with analytics.topUsers("submission_created", n) (highest count first, ties by learner id).

Input (stdin, JSON): a list of steps: { "submit": { "userId": "u_an", "challengeId": "c_17", "status": 202, "query": "&attempt=2" } } (userId null without a session), { "simulate": { "learners": 10000, "perLearner": 2, "challenges": 40 } }, { "total": true }, { "top": 3 }, { "series": true } and { "analytics": true }. The runner prints the total of the counter ("total: 6"), the top list ("top 3: u_an 3, u_chi 2, u_binh 1"), the number of series of the counter (and the series themselves when there are at most 12) and the submission_created events in the sink. Do not change the types, FakeMeter, AnalyticsSink or the test runner. The public tests pass on the assistant''s code; the hidden tests count the series with 10,000 learners and check what reaches the analytics sink.', 'open', 'medium'::difficulty_question, 'fix_bug', 30, true, false)
