VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_otl_332'), 1, 'How many different values can user_id take on CodeDev next year? And url? Multiply them with the other labels: that is how many series the metrics backend has to keep for this one counter. Which of the four labels have a small, fixed set of values?'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_otl_332'), 2, 'Look at the object passed to this.submissions.add in onSubmission: each key is a label. The request already carries a value that names the route without the ids, and the status can be reduced to its class. Then look at the AnalyticsSink class at the bottom of the file: it already knows how to count events per user, so topLearners does not need the counter at all.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_otl_332'), 3, 'A similar case with other data: a counter of video plays labelled { video_id, viewer_id, quality } grows with every viewer. Keep { quality } (and the player version) on the counter, which tells you how many plays fail or buffer, and send { name: "video_played", userId: viewerId, properties: { videoId } } to the event pipeline, where "most active viewers" is a group-by over events. Anonymous viewers stay in the counter but do not become a fake user in the events.');
