    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_otl_411'), 'POST /submissions, rolling 28 days (2026-09-29 .. 2026-10-26)
all requests                                    12,493,000
  4xx (400 validation, 401, 403, 413, 422)          93,000
  5xx (500, 502, 503, 504)                          21,000
  2xx/3xx slower than 2 s                           10,500
  2xx/3xx within 2 s                            12,368,500

SLO: 99.5% of valid requests are good (not 5xx and answered within 2 s), rolling 28 days. 4xx are not valid events.

Error budget policy:
budget left >= 50%   ship as usual (canary 10% for 30 min)
budget left 25-50%   ship only with a 60 min canary and the on-call engineer watching
budget left < 25%    feature releases wait; reliability fixes and rollbacks only

Statement: "About half of the error budget is spent, so under this policy the grader release can ship today, with the 60-minute canary."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Valid requests = 12,493,000 - 93,000 = 12,400,000, so the budget is 0.5% x 12,400,000 = 62,000 bad requests. Bad requests = 21,000 (5xx) + 10,500 (slower than 2 s) = 31,500, which is 50.8% of the budget: 49.2% is left, in the 25-50% band of the policy. The release may go out, but with the longer canary. Two common slips change the answer: dividing by all 12,493,000 requests (a slightly larger budget) or forgetting the slow requests (only 34% spent, which would wrongly allow shipping as usual).', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_otl_411') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
